# PROJECT: MY CHRISTMAS WORLD
## Master Product Specification, UX/UI Design System and Technical Implementation Brief

You are the lead product designer, senior frontend engineer, Three.js specialist, game developer, backend architect and QA engineer responsible for building **My Christmas World**.

Your task is to design and implement a complete, functional, premium-quality, browser-based 3D Christmas world-building game.

Do not build a static landing page, a concept mockup, a collection of screenshots, or a non-interactive visual demo. Build a real web application in which users create, decorate, save and revisit their own persistent 3D Christmas worlds.

You are expected to write almost all of the code yourself, organize it into maintainable files, test it, fix errors and explain how to run it.

The application should be designed for eventual public launch, user accounts, cloud persistence, daily rewards, social sharing and a future paid AI video-generation feature.

Build the first production-oriented version with a clear distinction between implemented functionality, temporary prototypes and future features.

---

# 1. PRODUCT VISION

My Christmas World is a digital Christmas universe where every user owns a small piece of snowy land and gradually transforms it into a beautiful, personal Christmas world.

The experience should combine:

- The emotional magic of Christmas.
- The creativity of a building game.
- The satisfaction of collecting daily gifts.
- The freedom to design a personal miniature world.
- The beauty of a cinematic winter landscape.
- The motivation to return every day and expand the world.
- The ability to share beautiful images and, in a later version, cinematic videos on social media.

The application should feel like entering a small, peaceful, magical winter universe.

It should not feel like an ordinary website, an administration dashboard or a children's mobile game.

The visual quality should evoke a premium Christmas film, a high-end miniature architectural visualization and an atmospheric winter diorama.

The user should feel emotionally attached to the world they create.

## Core product promise

“Your own little Christmas world, growing one gift at a time.”

This is a product-design direction, not a requirement to display this sentence permanently in the interface.

## Main product principles

1. The world belongs to the user.
2. The user has creative freedom.
3. The world persists between visits.
4. Daily gifts encourage returning without forcing artificial complexity.
5. The 3D environment is the central experience.
6. The interface should remain elegant, calm and intuitive.
7. The application should work in a modern desktop and mobile browser.
8. Every major visible control must perform its advertised function.

