# 11. DAILY GIFT SYSTEM

Daily gifts are one of the most important retention mechanics.

The idea is that users return to their world regularly to collect a new decorative object and gradually build a richer environment.

## Gift experience

Display a visually prominent but restrained “Daily Gift” control.

When the user opens it:

- Show an elegant modal.
- Display the available gift options.
- Show attractive 3D previews or clear illustrated previews.
- Let the user choose one reward.
- Explain what will be added to the world.
- Confirm the selection.

When a gift is collected:

1. Record the reward.
2. Add the corresponding object to the user's world.
3. Save the updated world.
4. Display a short success animation.
5. Update the gift status.

The gift should appear in a sensible initial position, with the option to reposition it immediately.

## Daily reward rules

The production implementation must enforce the daily limit on the server or through a trusted database operation.

Do not rely solely on frontend state, browser time or local storage.

Store a unique reward record per user per eligible calendar day, according to a clearly defined timezone policy.

The user must not be able to collect unlimited rewards by refreshing the browser or changing client-side state.

The initial reward pool may include:

- Christmas tree.
- Gift box.
- Snowman.
- Train.
- Street lamp.
- Decorative house.
- Light string.
- Bench.
- Christmas market stall.
- Reindeer decoration.

Start with four or five choices per reward cycle.

Provide enough variation to keep the world-building experience interesting.

For the development environment, provide a clearly identified testing mode that allows the reward flow to be tested without weakening production reward rules.

