# 13. IMAGE EXPORT

Users should be able to export a high-quality image of their world.

The export must capture the actual rendered 3D scene.

It must not simply screenshot the surrounding interface.

## Initial export functionality

Implement:

- Export current view as PNG.
- A sensible default resolution.
- A clear download action.
- A filename such as `my-christmas-world.png`.
- Error handling if rendering or export fails.

Preserve the intended scene colors and lighting.

Ensure the rendering configuration supports canvas export.

Avoid external textures or assets with cross-origin restrictions that would taint the canvas and break image export.

## Future export options

Design for later support of:

- Landscape image.
- Square social media image.
- Vertical image for stories and TikTok covers.
- Higher-resolution rendering.
- Optional removal of the interface.
- User-selected camera composition.

Do not implement a complex export editor until the basic PNG export works reliably.

