# 16. PERFORMANCE AND TECHNICAL QUALITY

The game must remain usable on ordinary modern laptops and mobile devices.

## Performance principles

- Use instanced meshes for repeated trees, ornaments or particles where beneficial.
- Reuse geometries and materials.
- Avoid unnecessary React re-renders of the entire scene.
- Lazy-load large assets.
- Optimize GLB/GLTF models.
- Use appropriate texture sizes.
- Limit dynamic shadow-casting lights.
- Keep post-processing optional.
- Dispose of resources correctly when removing objects or unloading assets.
- Provide loading indicators for large assets.
- Handle WebGL errors gracefully.

Use quality settings that can be adjusted based on device capabilities.

Do not sacrifice the entire visual experience for performance, but avoid effects that make the app unusable.

## Error handling

Provide clear messages for:

- Failed login.
- Failed cloud save.
- Missing backend configuration.
- Failed asset loading.
- Failed image export.
- WebGL initialization failure.
- Network interruption.

Never silently ignore critical failures.

